      "keyInsight": "Amateur thinkers believe more of a good thing is always better. Master strategists know every system bends along a curve.\n\nPicture a state tax rate. Tax zero percent, and the treasury collects nothing.\n\nTax one hundred percent, and nobody works, so the treasury still collects nothing. The peak revenue sits somewhere in between.\n\nYet political factions behave as if society sits on a straight ramp. One side screams that slashing taxes always prints cash.\n\nThe other claims hiking taxes always funds schools. Both fall for the linear trap.\n\nIn reality, moving in either direction past the summit destroys value. Decisive leadership requires asking where you stand on the curve before you push the throttle.",
